    historical_tag: Some("The Pawnee Fork fight occurred in April 1867 during General Winfield Scott Hancock\'s campaign against the Plains tribes. Hancock\'s threat to burn a Cheyenne village prompted the evacuation of the village, and a detachment of cavalry under Lieutenant George Armstrong Custer skirmished with Cheyenne warriors along Pawnee Fork in western Kansas. The engagement underscored the rising tensions that would lead to the Medicine Lodge Treaty negotiations later that year."),
    citations: [
        /*[0]*/ "Leckie, William H. — The Military Conquest of the Southern Plains",
        /*[1]*/ "Chalfant, William Y. — Hancock\'s War",
        /*[2]*/ "National Park Service — Pawnee Fork Battlefield",
    ],
